From: aps3e-s26 <aps3e-s26@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:53:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] vk: persist the driver pipeline cache per game

main4 creates a VkPipelineCache but starts it empty every launch and drops
it on exit, so the Adreno/Xclipse driver recompiles every pipeline from
SPIR-V cold on each boot. Load it from the game's cache directory, discard
data written by another GPU/driver (header vendor/device/UUID check), and
write it back after the startup shader-cache load and on teardown. Android
often kills the process before teardown, hence the early flush.

The cache calls also went straight to the system loader instead of the
PFN table, which bypasses a custom (adrenotools) driver; route them
through the table.

Based on mercurious/aps3e 4b4e12f5c (upstream PR #122), reworked for
main4's shared pipe-compiler cache.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QHcVVDuR9mxorL6GkyZmzr
